  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing Durable Solutions to Internal Displacement in Vanuatu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project, &#x201c;Advancing Durable Solutions to Internal Displacement in Vanuatu&#x201d; co-implemented by IOM and UNDP in close partnership with the Government of Vanuatu. will address displacement needs that arise in the context of disasters, integrate development principles into the humanitarian response, and enhance the Government&#x2019;s capacity to address displacement risks and identify durable solutions. In line with the Action Agenda on Internal Displacement, the project will strengthen leadership to implement solutions for Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs), across institutional lines and through a &#x201c;whole-of-government&#x201d; and a &#x201c;whole of UN&#x201d; effort. This will be achieved through the development of National Durable Solution Guidelines that are aligned with international standards and pilot implementation at the local level to advance durable solutions for IDPs. This will be complemented by the development of a multi-year financing framework and legislative reviews 1) to inform legal reform for the identification of durable solutions and 2) to ensure the catalytic impact of current and future programming. The project will prioritize the views, needs, and capacities of IDPs and host communities and promote sustainable, nationally- owned solutions through targeted capacity building at both national and local levels to shape investments and measure progress towards solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
